      "writtenOn": "2026-09-18T12:01:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Currently, the xyz.openbmc_project.State.Leak.Detector interface in PDI only defines Normal and Abnormal states. It does not have a dedicated state or property for detecting faults in the sensor itself.\n\nBecause of this limitation, I followed the existing design pattern used for the HPM SMA leak detectors. On the HPM SMA, the hardware exposes two separate GPIOs via an I2C IO expander—one for the actual leak status and one for the sensor fault status. To represent this in OpenBMC, the Entity-Manager config creates two separate GPIOLeakDetector instances (e.g., Hpm0LeakDetector and Hpm0LeakDetectorFault).\n\nSince the Nvidia SMA leak sensor also provides both a leak status and a fault status (sensor short/open), I adopted the same approach here: instantiating a primary State.Leak.Detector object for the leak, and a secondary _Fault object for the fault, which is consistent with how the GPIO leak detectors handle it.",
      "parentUuid": "2502486c_760832e4",
      "revId": "b309cc829515592ce80a17a419bc2139100e73d7",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
